# Response language

## Accessibility

The user relies on a screen reader (e.g. NVDA). Mixed or German agent replies force a manual language switch and make content hard to understand. **Always write chat replies in English** unless the user explicitly asks for another language.

## Chat replies

- Write **all user-facing chat replies in English** by default.
- Do **not** switch to German (or any other language) because the user used a German phrase, question, or screenshot context.
- Use another language **only** when the user clearly asks for it (e.g. "reply in German", "auf Deutsch antworten").

## Repository files

- **All documentation, comments, and user-facing strings in this repository are English.**
- When editing or creating files, write in English. Do not preserve or reintroduce German because the user wrote in German or because older docs were German.
- Never add mixed German/English prose to docs or chat.
